@{
  ViewData["Title"] = "Transfer fee quotes";
}

<h1>FeeQuote</h1>
<p>
  FeeQuote prices customer payment transfers. Channels send a transfer
  (amount, currency, origin and destination country) and receive a quote with
  an itemised fee breakdown and the total to debit.
</p>

<h2>Try it</h2>
<p>
  The interactive quote form is a small React app served from
  <a href="/app/">/app/</a>. It calls the same API that channel systems use.
</p>

<h2>API</h2>
<p><code>POST /api/quotes</code> with a JSON body:</p>
<pre><code>{
  "amountCents": 123500,
  "currency": "AUD",
  "originCountry": "AU",
  "destinationCountry": "AU",
  "channel": "online"
}</code></pre>
<p>
  The response carries <code>feeCents</code>, <code>totalCents</code> and a
  <code>breakdown</code> array of labelled amounts, all in integer cents.
</p>

<h2>Reference data</h2>
<dl>
  <dt>Currencies</dt>
  <dd>@ViewData["Currencies"]</dd>
  <dt>Countries</dt>
  <dd>@ViewData["Countries"]</dd>
</dl>
